@keith-packard  - The minimal libc has zero support for `signal()`, and actually it's usefulness and behaviour is kind of a grey area for all libc's that Zephyr links against. On the other hand, I would like to at least provide something that 3rd party libraries such as this can link against... (i.e. the linked issue is for adding a Lua module)

Would it be wrong to add the following to the minimal libc?
```cpp
sighandler_t signal(int signo, sighandler_t handler)
{
    errno = ENOSYS;
    return SIG_ERR;
}
```

Maybe with an extra `Kconfig` to conditionally compile / link? Should it go into common libc? Certainly, if it is ever supported, it would need to be a common implementation regardless of the toolchain libc..
